applications include criminal investigation support systems that provide knowledge-based Q&A                         
[[10.12972_jdfr.2024.1.1.4]], and power standard knowledge generation [[10.52152_4073]]. The versatility of RAG is   
further demonstrated across diverse verticals. In digital archives, integrated systems combining semantic retrieval  
and retrieval enhancement have outperformed traditional methods in question-answering and recommendation tasks       
[[^10.70695_iaai202504a7]]. For biodiversity conservation, BioChat employs a Re-Ranker-based RAG framework to        
significantly improve factual accuracy and reduce hallucinations in species-related queries [[^10.3390_su18010396]]. 
In education, RAG is central to Intelligent Educational Agents and multi-persona AI tutors, where it grounds         
responses in verified curricula and reduces hallucination risks through provenance cues                              
[[^10.55041_ijsrem55690]][^10.3390_asi9010017]. Additionally, RAG architectures are proving effective for            
low-resource and morphologically complex languages, such as Turkish, where they enhance information precision and    
contextual relevance [[^10.22531_muglajsci.1781095]]. In business intelligence, RAG-enhanced sentiment analysis      
systems combine transformer-based classification with semantic similarity retrieval to provide deeper contextual     
insights into customer reviews [[^10.22214_ijraset.2025.76657]].                                                     
                                                                                                                     
 ## Multimodal and Specialized RAG                                                                                   
                                                                                                                     
 The scope of RAG is expanding into multimodal and specialized data types. Enhanced Multimodal RAG-LLM frameworks    
introduce structured scene graphs to improve visual question answering and object recognition in complex scenes      
[[10.48550_arxiv.2412.20927]]. For time series forecasting, TimeRAF employs a retrieval-augmented foundation model to
enhance zero-shot prediction by accessing customized knowledge bases [[10.48550_arxiv.2412.20810]]. Similarly, RAG is
applied in mobile edge computing to optimize resource allocation in dynamic wireless systems                         
[[10.48550_arxiv.2412.20820]].                                                                                       
                                                                                                                     
